<div class="Page__contentArea"><div>
<div id="b428d125"><section id="key-information" class="tDwjVFExbPlqwnaU86Wz"><div class="Fov3KMlE7osNR74JI44t"><div class="Wf6h4ZdN2S9XvO6RoMCf"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF tNNRbfeiPsdi3j_gpC7k">Key information</h2><ul class="dE8scaebAaiVDo4BSvWD jQbeCSjNzeFEwKyP9FS0"><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-check-circle"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Acclaimed staff</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark"><span>Kristiania&rsquo;s researchers in this field work internationally and have several prominent research groups.</span></div></div></li><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-check-circle"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Sought-after skills</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark"><span>There is a great shortage of candidates with this type of competence in the labor market.</span></div></div></li><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-check-circle"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Specialization</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark"><span>You can take elective subjects and tailor your master&rsquo;s degree to your interests.</span></div></div></li><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-error-circle"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Academic department</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark"><a href="/en/faculties/faculty-of-health-sciences-and-technology/">School of Economics, Innovation, and Technology</a></div></div></li><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-user"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Admission requirements</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark">Read more at the bottom of the page.</div></div></li><li class="iIoZpbf7rJjFaPayfYGd"><div class="i9mvzE2ZVt1U_mgl53yZ NBkadhPtSiaEbuC1H71t"><div class="_HPUHJNlNHRSzaUJfTVb"><span class="SvgIcon tA8I0a90PWzmxCh2AhM3"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-credit-card"></use></svg></span><h3 class="ecyElYvuOSSL_6pZBv9V">Tuition fees</h3></div><div class="cZ1dIE6oJgjjufj0oSwG RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark">58 900 kr per semester.&nbsp;<a href="/en/study-at-kristiania/price-overview/"><span>Additional information about prices can be found here.</span></a></div></div></li></ul><ul class="KdKtz5eB9ExUSDYJcdj8"><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Level"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-book"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">Master</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Start date"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-clock"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">Fall 2026</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Mode of study"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-activity"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">Full-time</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Points"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-award"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">120 Points</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="City"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-map-pin"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">Oslo</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Duration"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-calendar"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">2 years</span></div></li><li><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN lgn5jtFtWmCfY3jJKvE1 _YiOaSqqzZqBucsGKGGx U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5" title="Language"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-message-square"></use></svg></span><span class="usSRVYlqJnoDeG8iYItA">English</span></div></li></ul></div></div></section><script>(window.__reactProps = window.__reactProps || {})['b428d125-json'] = {"id":"key-information","title":{"value":"Key information"},"facts":[{"title":{"value":"Acclaimed staff"},"icon":"check-circle","content":{"value":"<span>Kristiania&rsquo;s researchers in this field work internationally and have several prominent research groups.</span>"}},{"title":{"value":"Sought-after skills"},"icon":"check-circle","content":{"value":"<span>There is a great shortage of candidates with this type of competence in the labor market.</span>"}},{"title":{"value":"Specialization"},"icon":"check-circle","content":{"value":"<span>You can take elective subjects and tailor your master&rsquo;s degree to your interests.</span>"}},{"title":{"value":"Academic department"},"icon":"error-circle","content":{"value":"<a href=\"/en/faculties/faculty-of-health-sciences-and-technology/\">School of Economics, Innovation, and Technology</a>"}},{"title":{"value":"Admission requirements"},"icon":"user","content":{"value":"Read more at the bottom of the page."}},{"title":{"value":"Tuition fees"},"icon":"credit-card","content":{"value":"58 900 kr per semester.&nbsp;<a href=\"/en/study-at-kristiania/price-overview/\"><span>Additional information about prices can be found here.</span></a>"}}],"tags":[{"title":"Level","icon":"book","value":"Master"},{"title":"Start date","icon":"clock","value":"Fall 2026"},{"title":"Mode of study","icon":"activity","value":"Full-time"},{"title":"Points","icon":"award","value":"120 Points"},{"title":"City","icon":"map-pin","value":"Oslo"},{"title":"Duration","icon":"calendar","value":"2 years"},{"title":"Language","icon":"message-square","value":"English"}]};</script></div>
</div><div>
<div id="4668a882"><section id="learning-outcomes" class="cwjtYbGmpj2Fc0XguMNM"><div class="Fov3KMlE7osNR74JI44t"><div class="Wf6h4ZdN2S9XvO6RoMCf"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF aZkJAbcjSQdYr77t8LV7">Learning Outcomes</h2><div class="zOMHtRvuigbQpkhq8l0i"><div class="FHwe9agruJdTg4dYFHN9"><div class="FktOVJkMpTVphR1rGeNp RichtextContent RichtextContent--light">The main goal of the master program is to train future cyber security professionals knowledgeable in areas of secure software development, IT governance, audit, and management, where it is necessary to protect critical systems and national infrastructure from versatile cyber threats. Upon completion, students will be able to undertake the leadership role in managing the organization's cyber security strategy and architect complex and secure DevOps processes with cloud integration.</p>
<p>With us, you get to study topics such as:</p>
<ul class="Richtext__ul">
<li>Secure Software Development</li>
<li>End-point and Cloud Security</li>
<li>Cyber Threat Intelligence</li>
<li>Cryptography and Blockchain</li>
<li>AI for Cyber Security</li>
</ul></div><button title="More about the course" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_940" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT f_wbJQigmJWOUtJRHvmX"><span class="visuallyHidden">More about the course</span><span class="SvgIcon Kw06kOpEjKtbccDsYKVG"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-plus-circle"></use></svg></span></button><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_940" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_941"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_941" class="visuallyHidden">More about the course</span><h3 class="vGAYXQ8qVh3muyCADVi0">More about the course</h3><div class="RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark">While attending the master program in cyber security, the educational model might include the following components to facilitate learning and skills enhancement:</p>
<ul class="Richtext__ul">
<li>Lectures to introduce the theoretical concepts and frameworks</li>
<li>Seminars, oral presentations, and group works give students an opportunity to present, discuss and argue upon topics and achieve results</li>
<li>Supervision and assessment to guide the learning process</li>
<li>Use cases work and project execution</li>
<li>Attendance of the specialized workshop offered by the research environment</li>
<li>Independent practice, lab work and exercises</li>
<li>Participation in the collaboration projects through the cyber security lab &ndash; both internally and externally</li>
<li>Industry consultations and coordination for better alignment with industry needs</li>
</ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="qB4kMuPluv5Id4WqPmfn"></div><div class="uMSWbISaLHTvPMbXhnYp"><div class="slJnKPGAAIKofsQwQBjL vPKYJ9xnnqorRitmkm3i R1wh_51Fi_Crd9RnsQsw"><picture><source sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (min-width: 768px) 552px" srcSet="/contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg?width=375 375w, /contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg?width=552 552w, /contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg?width=768 768w, /contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg?width=1536 1536w"/><img src="/contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg?width=552" alt="student koder på pc" style="object-position:51% 32%" loading="lazy"/></picture></div></div></div></div></div></section><script>(window.__reactProps = window.__reactProps || {})['4668a882-json'] = {"id":"learning-outcomes","title":{"value":"Learning Outcomes"},"content":{"value":"The main goal of the master program is to train future cyber security professionals knowledgeable in areas of secure software development, IT governance, audit, and management, where it is necessary to protect critical systems and national infrastructure from versatile cyber threats. Upon completion, students will be able to undertake the leadership role in managing the organization's cyber security strategy and architect complex and secure DevOps processes with cloud integration.</p>\n<p>With us, you get to study topics such as:</p>\n<ul class=\"Richtext__ul\">\n<li>Secure Software Development</li>\n<li>End-point and Cloud Security</li>\n<li>Cyber Threat Intelligence</li>\n<li>Cryptography and Blockchain</li>\n<li>AI for Cyber Security</li>\n</ul>"},"overlayTitle":"More about the course","overlayContent":{"value":"While attending the master program in cyber security, the educational model might include the following components to facilitate learning and skills enhancement:</p>\n<ul class=\"Richtext__ul\">\n<li>Lectures to introduce the theoretical concepts and frameworks</li>\n<li>Seminars, oral presentations, and group works give students an opportunity to present, discuss and argue upon topics and achieve results</li>\n<li>Supervision and assessment to guide the learning process</li>\n<li>Use cases work and project execution</li>\n<li>Attendance of the specialized workshop offered by the research environment</li>\n<li>Independent practice, lab work and exercises</li>\n<li>Participation in the collaboration projects through the cyber security lab &ndash; both internally and externally</li>\n<li>Industry consultations and coordination for better alignment with industry needs</li>\n</ul>"},"gobiStoryId":null,"imageFallback":{"author":null,"caption":null,"url":"/contentassets/29a98a3dc2bb4144b24840a288147234/gobi-placeholder-tek.jpg","alt":"student koder på pc","focalPoint":{"x":0.51,"y":0.32},"lazyLoading":true},"translations":{"openOverlay":"More about the course","closeOverlay":"Close overlay","openPlayer":"Open player","failedToLoadVideo":"Sorry, for some reason we could not load a video"}};</script></div>
</div><div>
<div id="d522e80d"><section id="study-model" class="eXDLkCBTey4RjrTQSVwU"><div class="coBlOy78vCNQoCaBJMWq"><div class="fIm4MtcrG6MCKKd8iidQ"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF A9Jn0XOSrtngUTCr8gcL">Study model</h2><div class="t78ozlVAuwJUrQItlgiY"><span class="IKcqvZpEOT2PNX0vgEn0">The Master&#x27;s degree runs over two years and consists of a total of 120 ECTS.</span></div></div></div><div class="DwbrqOYPLpXMxa_AUi5a"><div class="c4EHzShG0bxjcWsv1iba _jn80nJpcKPRabCSPcI8 o7i_4ji7xZ2pdim0DGGS r6PBO9Z23nGvfMtmlwMK dT6kOO1SWAAgm3_8NHMn"><div class="w6rdwzyeKdZC4QEQQdUG"><div class="FQnvPH3eSTnAU6bvrkhn"><div class="IbD8iYA8j6gRUkFt19Qt nUUm_USrpFGrNosOvcCN gXLqKND3fX0_VG9NQewb"><div role="tablist" class="_NQp5NLSF5eDFXAqjrMf" aria-label="Select year"><button id="tab_1" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabPanel_1" type="button" class="wSwA7V6mKnVhr5xFafzq Sqayds_IfbVRGAlPcZz1"><span class="bAoReRDLMgoAniQxqdep">First year</span></button><button id="tab_2" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabPanel_2" type="button" class="wSwA7V6mKnVhr5xFafzq"><span class="bAoReRDLMgoAniQxqdep">Second year</span></button></div></div><span class="FaaFQQsQ1uH8384yNffh">120 total credits</span></div><div id="tabPanel_1" class="xD2nuHiyJc0KNBTM5TWg" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab_1"><div class="XtdQZg9bKtEzGXT39oxb"><div style="will-change:height;overflow:hidden;visibility:hidden;height:0" class="wpyTqNTlEGsGZ_xfFehk BK3qq6WSy_IM14HivUP2"><div class="XjUXAnCLxrJU_S3Faibn km5O6Vr04dX9qXqlrGMV Wc0G2UOdAM4L2tA07AtA"><div id="comboSelect_id1187" class="bbDHU4_JdA0hl9MD1Lrq">Options:</div><fieldset aria-describedby="comboSelect_id1187"><div class="drG0qWE9kXwq4x52jnrJ"><div class="Sp19XW4DI_sJH0_4zvTF"><div class="PHAoRS_eP5FouDCPNKdY GhAWyApR_JjGprSMJ2rM yje2hGysH1zQf_D0GsA7 echijgywrVRRk64pe6Cg"><input type="radio" id="FormComponents__radio__1188" class="YfHgbQjwjs4O8VWhll1c" name="study-option-selector" checked="" value="Default path"/><label for="FormComponents__radio__1188" class="XTEgAUAWtLfl5XRg_bT7"><span class="yUjgOv16CeoVvFj3U4nh">Default path</span></label></div><div class="PHAoRS_eP5FouDCPNKdY GhAWyApR_JjGprSMJ2rM yje2hGysH1zQf_D0GsA7 echijgywrVRRk64pe6Cg"><input type="radio" id="FormComponents__radio__1189" class="YfHgbQjwjs4O8VWhll1c" name="study-option-selector" value="Default path"/><label for="FormComponents__radio__1189" class="XTEgAUAWtLfl5XRg_bT7"><span class="yUjgOv16CeoVvFj3U4nh">Exchange</span></label></div></div></div></fieldset></div></div><span class="NPFkgrIiXfIBoY50mCiN">60 credits</span><div class="osNFPrEfj_WDLlms79Vw"><div class="gIhCJK5vlYW4N6yeTlUe C70d_1unGsLcavciTBWP g8GJRoyN3YYrck7buLCF" style="grid-template-columns:auto repeat(4, minmax(min-content, 1fr))"><div class="PVTUTdX7fee_uJTuRkiD ihFnGka9xDug5NPWFh0C"></div><div class="PH6z9gi7b9kHBB9jOhSt nPbPqGrz5Ue0OKa68YnY z7vhCTYrC3rO2VoUPlYT">1. semester</div><div class="PH6z9gi7b9kHBB9jOhSt nPbPqGrz5Ue0OKa68YnY _MLObcIsnBTnfP4F5AQg">2. semester</div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:3 / span 1;grid-row:1"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1190" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Secure Software Development</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MC100</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1190" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1191"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1191" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Secure Software Development</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>Modern software is a very complex system performing varieties of tasks such as data analysis in healthcare systems, analyzing camera images in self-driving cars and even controlling gates in water dams. With increasing complexity, it is imperative to understand and integrate cybersecurity in every aspect of the software development lifecycle. The objective of the course is to give students understanding of the core cybersecurity principles in CD/CI as well as DevSecOps to plan, develop and manage agile software products. </p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:4 / span 1;grid-row:1"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1192" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">End-Point and Cloud Security</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MC101</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1192" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1193"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1193" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">End-Point and Cloud Security</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>The goal of the course is to give students understanding of the fundamental methods and tools to be used in security for a whole range of solutions, from smaller Internet of Things applications to large-scale cloud systems. It is no longer a simple one-dimensional approach to deployment of the intrusion detection or antivirus programs, yet rather an orchestration of multiple tools. The students will learn how to navigate, deploy, manage and monitor networks using conventional solutions as well as cloud solutions with defense-in-depth principle and share responsibilities.</p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:5 / span 1;grid-row:1"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1194" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Cyber Threat Intelligence</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MC102</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1194" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1195"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1195" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Cyber Threat Intelligence</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>Information has an extreme value when collected and applied in a relevant and timely manner. The students will learn how to operate with the threat’s information, open-source intelligence, social network intelligence, forensics analysis of the artifacts and log files. They will also master skills in applying the attribution and basic triage based on the internationally recognized frameworks, such that MITRE ATT&CK. </p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:2 / span 1;grid-row:1"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1196" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Ethics, Sustainability and Society</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MA141</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1196" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1197"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1197" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Ethics, Sustainability and Society</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>The main aim of this course is to provide students with the fundamental knowledge of ethics and sustainability necessary for responsible innovation and the development of new information technologies (IT) in the modern society. The central topics include the role of ethics in responsible innovation and IT development; information privacy concerns, social, economic, and environmental impacts of innovations and new ITs; and how IT development and innovation can contribute to achieving the UN Sustainable Development Goals. In covering ethical and sustainability issues, the course addresses the perspectives of various stakeholders at the individual level (IT developers, innovators, consumers, investors), the organizational level (commercial, public, and non-governmental organizations), and the societal level (local and regional communities, nations, international society). Group work on possible solutions to real-life ethical and sustainability challenges constitutes an essential part of the course.</p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:2 / span 1;grid-row:3"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1198" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Cryptography and Blockchain</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MC103</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1198" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1199"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1199" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Cryptography and Blockchain</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>Blockchain has revolutionized many facets of daily life, from finance to healthcare. This technology relies on advanced cryptographic techniques. While it offers immense benefits for societal advancement, it's essential to grasp the nuances of cryptographic applications to safeguard system security and uphold individual privacy. Students will delve into concepts of data-in-transit and data-at-rest encryption, learn to scrutinize Bitcoin transactions, and understand how to seamlessly integrate prevalent blockchain solutions.</p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:3 / span 1;grid-row:3"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1200" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">AI for Cyber Security</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MC104</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1200" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1201"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1201" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">AI for Cyber Security</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>Cybersecurity has become an integral component of our digitized existence. As the number of connected devices grows, so does the volume of data, which may conceal evidence of cyberattacks or illicit activities. It is not only challenging for human experts to process this vast amount of information but also nearly impossible to capture every nuance and context of potential cyber threats. In this course, students will explore foundational AI concepts and models, such as clustering, classification, and regression. These tools can be leveraged across various cybersecurity domains. These encompass, but aren't limited to, analyzing computer viruses, monitoring network traffic, and investigating financial crimes. By harnessing AI, we can enhance the speed and efficiency of data processing, a feature that many contemporary industrial cybersecurity solutions are swiftly adopting.</p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:4 / span 1;grid-row:3"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1202" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Research Methods</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">MS321</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1202" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1203"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1203" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Research Methods</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>This course is intended as a master level introduction to research methodology and the research process. This introduction gives the students an overview of the basic concept, methods, and practice of research. </p><p>Research is a cyclical process where new and carefully planned investigations build and extend on established work. The aim is to provide students with a fundamental understanding of research as a conceptual, empirical, and practical approach to gathering new insight and knowledge. The content provides a broad overview of how researchers work within the fields of economy, innovation, and technology. It presents students with relevant methods from these domains, along with their possibilities and limitations. </p><p>Students will learn a systematic approach to empirical investigation, including literature search, research design and methodology, qualitative and quantitative analyses, and the presentation and evaluation of results. </p><p>At completion of the course, students will be able to study and interpret existing research on a topic and suggest approaches to broaden or deepen knowledge within a given topic.</p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="Ka1VIQ2BSAPjauIEHrxP" style="grid-column:5 / span 1;grid-row:3"><div role="none" class="jkzRoAa60jRsn7WFC38b W_ipeNxzDR7tVIgpSCZn" tabindex="-1"><h3 class="YG1nlAZdhHLMRy9GYzR4"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="overlay_1204" aria-haspopup="dialog" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT H8BBXS4M_AkAanZLMEqS"><div class="Lv5sVd5u45Hei4dM91D6"><span class="cLkCE07zhLnMWRjri1dT">Proposal Development</span><span class="scgJDiGbZP69e6JD2e1j">PDE5100</span></div></button></h3><div class="k1UzcGuDdqoVJEx_3umq"><div class="QfpSu3R9osOn5mtmUmRN AK7QRdIj4UViy_jglQrq jno52DfczcFYoXwAJOAu U9uDXh99G9DWi_Yh96aO EPjsXy4Ah89AtUfpopbN Iga6BKVCOIbIKJLg1wb5 RNsXkIAukZjr8f4x_HXA iFv6rrcS3ouLeLPVmLv7">7.5<!-- --> <!-- -->credits</div></div></div><div style="display:none"><div class="QhFNlQLYGSl_aaOQtwwl" style="display:none" id="overlay_1204" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="overlayLabel_1205"><div class="lAKZZQugItoUqTlu8DRV"></div><div tabindex="-1"><div class="po18YUo5kkFOZqsiTnKR"><div class="eOdUoHIpgD7QwsaR1kGn"><button title="Close overlay" type="button" class="NtmtjnwY8FdZxOUBkRwT sZg2Vy20YIsqTNv9TcIX"><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-circle-close"></use></svg></span><span class="visuallyHidden">Close overlay</span></button></div><div class="fyYha0cYX3WzsCpMkhUB"><span id="overlayLabel_1205" class="visuallyHidden">Open subject overlay</span><div><h3 class="E3lyE2pUr4JODpEYbHMe">Proposal Development</h3><div class="vyo8UTe2MiSR4m0iLBYR">
<p>The overall objective of this course is to help students conceptualize and prepare a timely and relevant research proposal, and to nurture a sense of inquisitiveness and active participation in research. The course aims at offering insight into the process behind a successful research project. It has an applied approach that involves collaborative and reciprocal partnerships between the university (faculty, staff, and/or students) and external communities for the mutually beneficial exchange of knowledge and resources. The research proposal forms the basis for the master thesis and the allocation of supervisor(s). </p>
</div><div class="iCNqjCRL4lMHUFqVaQaB"><button disabled="" type="button" class="yEK9biWpMxeKit4W3SEn HIBx2TMQpGodNFRbYUAk Pf5HgbFCxXwoDDfyfLsp cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE yWrwquZkc56N0bYjqb7s"><span>Read more</span><span class="SvgIcon"><svg><use xlink:href="/dist/iconsSprite.ff403ecca.svg#sprite-arrow-right"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="hUrOK4f2t5d89i_al5eu _jBcyRZzOe6QMtbojFs5"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="_qtIUhem1sc1EKjP4UhQ"><div id="tabPanel_2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab_2"><ul><li><span>MS404</span><span>Master&#x27;s Thesis</span><div>
<p>The master's thesis is a research project in which students will apply the knowledge acquired during their studies. It is a crafted scholarly document presenting research questions and original arguments based on scientific methods under the guidance of an advisor. The choice of topic and the methods used should be informed by the field of study. The thesis gives the student the opportunity to demonstrate expertise in their chosen research area. Students will acquire specialized problem-solving skills, be able to plan and conduct the steps in the research and/or development process at a high methodological standard. They shall take responsibility to conduct a well planned and executed project. </p>
</div></li><li><span>UTV999-MA-30</span><span>Utveksling</span><div></div></li><li><span>VALUTV99930M</span><span>Elective courses or exchange studies</span><div>
<p style="text-indent:0pt;margin-left:0pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-right:0pt;">See <a href="https://www.kristiania.no/for-studenter/valgemner-og-praksis/" style="color:#0000EE;text-decoration:underline ;">elective courses</a> or <a href="https://www.kristiania.no/en/for-students/outgoing-exchange-students/" style="color:#0000EE;text-decoration:underline ;">exchange opportunities</a>.</p>
</div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><div class="lv4eNMiZgLixMXhAvacD"><a href="/en/syllabus/faculty-of-health-sciences-and-technology/second-cycle-degree/mcs/master-in-cyber-security/" class="XezMfDvRba8HKhHr79wm UssovIOXlEuxxbOHY4c4 AMdryBi_G8WFVbcuUzSv LVwfmt8Qy2xfZW7GrHx_ I0dQ9KoNo8oj51pfedVE cJMgeHEGyMPOPNoeRPfY SwVWunM8J0KL5d8Ov54G" data-owned=""><div class="DdPYOTimBd1c8zDeoFgi">See program description</div></a></div></section><script>(window.__reactProps = window.__reactProps || {})['d522e80d-json'] = {"heading":{"value":"Study model"},"getSubjectInfoUrl":"/api/study-pages/94543/subjects-info-url","overlayContentMessages":{"outdated":{"heading":"Subjected to change.","message":null,"variant":"info"},"fallback":{"heading":"Course description coming soon","message":{"value":"At Kristiania, we develop our studies in collaboration with working life. That's why we update the subjects regularly, so that you get the skills that employers are looking for. Soon you can read everything about this subject here, until then you will find more information in the study programme description."},"variant":"info"}},"subjects":[{"code":"MA141","name":"Ethics, Sustainability and Society","description":"\n<p>The main aim of this course is to provide students with the fundamental knowledge of ethics and sustainability necessary for responsible innovation and the development of new information technologies (IT) in the modern society. The central topics include the role of ethics in responsible innovation and IT development; information privacy concerns, social, economic, and environmental impacts of innovations and new ITs; and how IT development and innovation can contribute to achieving the UN Sustainable Development Goals. In covering ethical and sustainability issues, the course addresses the perspectives of various stakeholders at the individual level (IT developers, innovators, consumers, investors), the organizational level (commercial, public, and non-governmental organizations), and the societal level (local and regional communities, nations, international society). Group work on possible solutions to real-life ethical and sustainability challenges constitutes an essential part of the course.</p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":14,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MC100","name":"Secure Software Development","description":"\n<p>Modern software is a very complex system performing varieties of tasks such as data analysis in healthcare systems, analyzing camera images in self-driving cars and even controlling gates in water dams. With increasing complexity, it is imperative to understand and integrate cybersecurity in every aspect of the software development lifecycle. The objective of the course is to give students understanding of the core cybersecurity principles in CD/CI as well as DevSecOps to plan, develop and manage agile software products. </p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":11,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MC101","name":"End-Point and Cloud Security","description":"\n<p>The goal of the course is to give students understanding of the fundamental methods and tools to be used in security for a whole range of solutions, from smaller Internet of Things applications to large-scale cloud systems. It is no longer a simple one-dimensional approach to deployment of the intrusion detection or antivirus programs, yet rather an orchestration of multiple tools. The students will learn how to navigate, deploy, manage and monitor networks using conventional solutions as well as cloud solutions with defense-in-depth principle and share responsibilities.</p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":12,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MC102","name":"Cyber Threat Intelligence","description":"\n<p>Information has an extreme value when collected and applied in a relevant and timely manner. The students will learn how to operate with the threat’s information, open-source intelligence, social network intelligence, forensics analysis of the artifacts and log files. They will also master skills in applying the attribution and basic triage based on the internationally recognized frameworks, such that MITRE ATT&CK. </p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":13,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MC103","name":"Cryptography and Blockchain","description":"\n<p>Blockchain has revolutionized many facets of daily life, from finance to healthcare. This technology relies on advanced cryptographic techniques. While it offers immense benefits for societal advancement, it's essential to grasp the nuances of cryptographic applications to safeguard system security and uphold individual privacy. Students will delve into concepts of data-in-transit and data-at-rest encryption, learn to scrutinize Bitcoin transactions, and understand how to seamlessly integrate prevalent blockchain solutions.</p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":21,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"second","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MC104","name":"AI for Cyber Security","description":"\n<p>Cybersecurity has become an integral component of our digitized existence. As the number of connected devices grows, so does the volume of data, which may conceal evidence of cyberattacks or illicit activities. It is not only challenging for human experts to process this vast amount of information but also nearly impossible to capture every nuance and context of potential cyber threats. In this course, students will explore foundational AI concepts and models, such as clustering, classification, and regression. These tools can be leveraged across various cybersecurity domains. These encompass, but aren't limited to, analyzing computer viruses, monitoring network traffic, and investigating financial crimes. By harnessing AI, we can enhance the speed and efficiency of data processing, a feature that many contemporary industrial cybersecurity solutions are swiftly adopting.</p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":21,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"second","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MS321","name":"Research Methods","description":"\n<p>This course is intended as a master level introduction to research methodology and the research process. This introduction gives the students an overview of the basic concept, methods, and practice of research. </p><p>Research is a cyclical process where new and carefully planned investigations build and extend on established work. The aim is to provide students with a fundamental understanding of research as a conceptual, empirical, and practical approach to gathering new insight and knowledge. The content provides a broad overview of how researchers work within the fields of economy, innovation, and technology. It presents students with relevant methods from these domains, along with their possibilities and limitations. </p><p>Students will learn a systematic approach to empirical investigation, including literature search, research design and methodology, qualitative and quantitative analyses, and the presentation and evaluation of results. </p><p>At completion of the course, students will be able to study and interpret existing research on a topic and suggest approaches to broaden or deepen knowledge within a given topic.</p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":23,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"second","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"MS404","name":"Master's Thesis","description":"\n<p>The master's thesis is a research project in which students will apply the knowledge acquired during their studies. It is a crafted scholarly document presenting research questions and original arguments based on scientific methods under the guidance of an advisor. The choice of topic and the methods used should be informed by the field of study. The thesis gives the student the opportunity to demonstrate expertise in their chosen research area. Students will acquire specialized problem-solving skills, be able to plan and conduct the steps in the research and/or development process at a high methodological standard. They shall take responsibility to conduct a well planned and executed project. </p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":61,"points":30,"year":2,"semester":"second","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"PDE5100","name":"Proposal Development","description":"\n<p>The overall objective of this course is to help students conceptualize and prepare a timely and relevant research proposal, and to nurture a sense of inquisitiveness and active participation in research. The course aims at offering insight into the process behind a successful research project. It has an applied approach that involves collaborative and reciprocal partnerships between the university (faculty, staff, and/or students) and external communities for the mutually beneficial exchange of knowledge and resources. The research proposal forms the basis for the master thesis and the allocation of supervisor(s). </p>\n","isDescriptionOutdated":false,"order":24,"points":7.5,"year":1,"semester":"second","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":null,"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"UTV999-MA-30","name":"Utveksling","description":null,"isDescriptionOutdated":null,"order":1,"points":30,"year":2,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":{"label":"Exchange","isDefault":false},"category":"obligatory"},{"code":"VALUTV99930M","name":"Elective courses or exchange studies","description":"\r\n<p style=\"text-indent:0pt;margin-left:0pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-right:0pt;\">See <a href=\"https://www.kristiania.no/for-studenter/valgemner-og-praksis/\" style=\"color:#0000EE;text-decoration:underline ;\">elective courses</a> or <a href=\"https://www.kristiania.no/en/for-students/outgoing-exchange-students/\" style=\"color:#0000EE;text-decoration:underline ;\">exchange opportunities</a>.</p>\r\n","isDescriptionOutdated":true,"order":1,"points":30,"year":2,"semester":"first","isPrerequisite":false,"specialization":null,"studyOption":{"label":"Default path","isDefault":true},"category":"elective"}],"translations":{"studyOptions":"Options","elective":"Elective","specialization":"Specialization","selectYear":"Select year","openSubjectOverlay":"Open subject overlay","closeOverlay":"Close overlay","genericErrorMessage":"Error occured","totalStudyPointsFormat":"{points} total credits","studyPointsFormat":"{points} credits","pointsUnit":"credits","noSubjectsMessage":"Sorry, the content could not be loaded at the moment","prerequisites":"Prerequisites","goToSubject":"Read more","loading":"Loading data","year":"year","semester":"semester","single":"single","first":"first","second":"second","third":"third","fourth":"fourth","fifth":"fifth"},"type":"view","id":"study-model","teaser":"The Master's degree runs over two years and consists of a total of 120 ECTS.","settings":{"disableStudyModel":false,"disabledStudyModelHeading":"Study model information","disabledStudyModelMessage":{"value":"The study model is being worked on and will be published as soon as it is ready"}},"studyProgramLink":{"label":"See program description","href":"/en/syllabus/faculty-of-health-sciences-and-technology/second-cycle-degree/mcs/master-in-cyber-security/","external":false,"showIsExternal":true}};</script></div>
</div><div>
<div id="12673250"><section id="career-opportunities" class="cr4GKFNCqp2Yu1c2kbOA"><div class="Fov3KMlE7osNR74JI44t"><div class="Wf6h4ZdN2S9XvO6RoMCf"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF vw2qEzBLsG8dfPFKhCCL">Career Opportunities</h2><div class="eCTirCs_JIAXtZrCECpB"><div class="s4PUgF87xJpwYCH4qegZ"><div class="gOFfCOGgsoYfQDsrulwN Um_bsxrmr048dYBfonAO hfMRvjcJ6bvRCr56YbNA"><div class="KgSPjnWKLeiPJ0FM0dQy RichtextContent RichtextContent--dark">With this master's degree, you qualify for positions such as:</p>
<ul class="Richtext__ul">
<li>Cyber security consultant</li>
<li>Security Engineer</li>
<li>DevSecOps engineer</li>
<li>Chief Information Security Office</li>
<li>Chief Information Officer</li>
</ul>
<p><br />As a Cyber Security specialist, you&rsquo;ll have several career opportunities within fields such as information security risk management and IT governance, quantum computing security and cryptography, IoT (Internet of Things) security and security cloud orchestration, protection against ransomware and reverse engineering.</div><div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><script>(window.__reactProps = window.__reactProps || {})['12673250-json'] = {"id":"career-opportunities","heading":{"value":"Career Opportunities"},"teaser":{"value":"With this master's degree, you qualify for positions such as:</p>\n<ul class=\"Richtext__ul\">\n<li>Cyber security consultant</li>\n<li>Security Engineer</li>\n<li>DevSecOps engineer</li>\n<li>Chief Information Security Office</li>\n<li>Chief Information Officer</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br />As a Cyber Security specialist, you&rsquo;ll have several career opportunities within fields such as information security risk management and IT governance, quantum computing security and cryptography, IoT (Internet of Things) security and security cloud orchestration, protection against ransomware and reverse engineering."},"linkList":[],"featuredArticle":null,"blockVariant":"default","overlayButtonLabel":null,"overlayHeading":null,"overlayContent":null,"overlayCloseLabel":"Close overlay"};</script></div>
</div><div>
<div id="75734de0"><section id="meet-the-faculty" class="xfIZ8IPRSKGxzL5KIyLz ZG9x_vn8GvsrSWPis7bl"><div class="Fov3KMlE7osNR74JI44t"><div class="Wf6h4ZdN2S9XvO6RoMCf"><h2 class="FrR9v_ssranAjR5kDzwF Bje8lNYEARjKXkaadcjl">Meet the faculty</h2><div class="IP4WLEZAtSgblGP4Felg"><div class="KCVvuotjBI0iy0ATTKfK"><div class="slJnKPGAAIKofsQwQBjL vPKYJ9xnnqorRitmkm3i ssmQS4h9jzEH4V0L4NSN"><picture><source sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (min-width: 768px) 552px" srcSet="/contentassets/d1fbb86e13d74cad8e0e1cf85bcfba3c/master-human-computer-interaction-1.jpg?width=375 375w, /contentassets/d1fbb86e13d74cad8e0e1cf85bcfba3c/master-human-computer-interaction-1.jpg?width=552 552w, /contentassets/d1fbb86e13d74cad8e0e1cf85bcfba3c/master-human-computer-interaction-1.jpg?width=768 768w, /contentassets/d1fbb86e13d74cad8e0e1cf85bcfba3c/master-human-computer-interaction-1.jpg?width=1536 1536w"/><img src="/contentassets/d1fbb86e13d74cad8e0e1cf85bcfba3c/master-human-computer-interaction-1.jpg?width=552" alt="Bildet viser en mannlig foreleser som står foran en gruppe studenter i et klasserom. Han står ved en skjerm som viser ordene &quot;Augmented Reality&quot;. Studentene, som hovedsakelig er sett bakfra, bruker bærbare datamaskiner, noe som antyder at de tar notater eller deltar aktivt i leksjonen. Klasserommet ser moderne ut, med lyse vinduer i bakgrunnen." style="object-position:50% 39%" loading="lazy"/></picture></div></div><ul class="tZx0pZhK8q3JNoQI8LCj"><li class="i8yQuD9MeLJCD5eDKft2"><div class="cVALO6yJDjmV1Xvkvynu"><div class="WWUAFGePNJBA0_seRWlX"><h3 class="TCpxq20heJlGBaSbNI4y">How we work</h3><div class="AXbF9ehRSXzzERBwn1XK RichtextContent RichtextContent--light">Our research emphasizes economics, innovation, digitization and IT. In addition, there are several exciting research projects in applied informatics, information systems and human-computer interaction.&nbsp;Our lecturers have extensive experience both within industry and academia. Relevant working life experience is brought into the teaching through lecturing and guest lecturing. This&nbsp;will make you used to working life challenges and will ease the transition between study life and work life.</p>
<p><!-- [if gte mso 9]><xml>
